# MQL5 Puria Method MA MACD

## Source
- Source: [[sources/mql5-codebase-mt5-strategies]]
- Page / Timestamp: MQL5 CodeBase, "Puria method - expert for MetaTrader 5", idea by Sergey Deev, code by Vladimir Karputov / barabashkakvn, published 2019-01-02, https://www.mql5.com/en/code/23250

## Mechanics

### Entry
- Baseline symbols: EURUSD.DWX first, then liquid DWX FX majors.
- Timeframe: M30 baseline, matching the source's EURUSD M30 test note.
- Use all ticks = false for deterministic new-bar operation.
- Short setup:
  - Fast MA is above both slow MAs by more than 0.5 points.
  - MACD confirmation is bearish according to source-code direction.
  - Enter short on the next bar.
- Long setup:
  - Fast MA is below both slow MAs by more than 0.5 points.
  - MACD confirmation is bullish according to source-code direction.
  - Enter long on the next bar.
- Note: the source explicitly describes the method as selling when fast MA moves above the two slow MAs; V5 keeps that contrarian Puria direction.

### Exit
- Close on opposite full setup.
- Source partial-close and breakeven features are disabled in the baseline.
- Baseline TP = 2R.

### Stop Loss
- V5 baseline: SL = 1.5 x ATR(14), unless source-code fixed SL default is adopted during build review.

### Position Sizing
- V5 baseline: fixed-risk $1,000 per backtest trade.
- Live sizing deferred to V5 risk conventions.

### Additional filters
- One-position-per-magic.
- Partial closure disabled.
- Breakeven move disabled in baseline; may be a later fixed variant.
- V5 default spread guard.
- No grid, martingale, averaging, or adaptive sizing.

